STATUTORY CORPORATION
Features of Statutory Corporation
Formation: It is established under a special Act of the parliament,
that lays down the objects, powers and functions of the
Corporation.
Ownership: It is wholly owned by the government. Government has
the power to appropriate its profits and also has to bear the losses,
if any.
Corporate Existence: A statutory corporation is a body corporate,
which has a separate legal existence independent of the
Government. It can sue and be sued, enter into contract and
acquire property in its own name.
