STATUTORY CORPORATION
Features of Statutory Corporation
Financial Autonomy: This type of enterprise is usually
independently financed. It obtains funds by borrowings from the
government or through revenues derived from sale of goods and
services to public.
Accounting and audit procedures: It is not subject to the
government rules and regulations in the matter of accounting,
budgeting and audit as applicable to departmental
undertakings,
Staffing and Terms of Service: The public corporation has its own
rules of recruitment and remuneration for its staffs and
employees.
